 ### Requirement: Muted Peer Highlighting when Same Lemma is ON
-When `Lemma` highlighting is ON, selecting a token in the text panel SHALL apply primary active highlight styling (`.highlight-orange-active` or `.highlight-purple-active`) to the clicked token (and any compound sibling bound to the same compound occurrence), and secondary muted highlight styling (`.lemma-peer-highlight`) to all other occurrences and tokens in the document that share any of its constituent lemmas. Secondary muted peer highlights (`.lemma-peer-highlight`) SHALL persist across user cursor movements and mouseout events over other text words, and SHALL NOT be cleared on mouseout. When selecting an individual constituent subtoken of a compound, the system SHALL restrict active lemma activation strictly to the clicked subtoken's atomic lemma and SHALL NOT activate parent compound lemmas, preventing unrelated subtoken components (such as single-letter prefixes) from receiving peer highlighting. Selecting a row in `#lemma-table` SHALL apply primary active highlight styling to all constituent occurrences of that lemma in the active sentence chunk. Clicking an already-highlighted constituent token in the text SHALL immediately deselect the lemma and clear all active and peer highlights without requiring multiple clicks.
+When `Lemma` highlighting is ON, selecting a token in the text panel SHALL apply primary active highlight styling (`.highlight-orange-active` or `.highlight-purple-active`) to the clicked token (and any compound or separable sibling bound to the same compound occurrence), and secondary muted highlight styling (`.lemma-peer-highlight`, retaining muted amber background `rgba(210, 153, 34, 0.25)` and `1px dashed` outline) to all other occurrences and tokens in the document that share any of its constituent lemmas. Secondary muted peer highlights (`.lemma-peer-highlight`) SHALL persist across user cursor movements and mouseout events over other text words, and SHALL NOT be cleared on mouseout. When selecting an individual constituent subtoken of a compound, the system SHALL restrict active lemma activation strictly to the clicked subtoken's atomic lemma and SHALL NOT activate parent compound lemmas, preventing unrelated subtoken components (such as single-letter prefixes) from receiving peer highlighting. Selecting a row in `#lemma-table` SHALL apply primary active highlight styling (`.highlight-orange-active` or `.highlight-purple-active`) strictly to the primary occurrence of that row (and any bound partner of that primary occurrence), and SHALL apply `.lemma-peer-highlight` to all non-primary occurrences of that row or lemma across both intra-sentence and multi-sentence texts. Toggling `#kw-btn-same-lemma` while a table row is selected SHALL dynamically add or remove `.lemma-peer-highlight` on those non-primary occurrences in real time without changing the primary occurrence's active highlight. Clicking an already-highlighted constituent token in the text SHALL immediately deselect the lemma and clear all active and peer highlights without requiring multiple clicks.
 
